Subject: [PATCH] nuttx: include tls_task.h for the task TLS API

task_tls_alloc / task_tls_get_value / task_tls_set_value are declared in
nuttx/tls_task.h, and nuttx/tls.h does not pull it in.  The NuttX port
only includes tls.h, so on a NuttX where the task TLS API lives in its
own header the build fails with implicit-declaration errors:

  libuv/src/unix/nuttx.c: error: implicit declaration of function
      'task_tls_alloc' [-Werror=implicit-function-declaration]

Only shows up once CONFIG_TLS_TASK_NELEM is non-zero, which is why the
default configurations do not hit it.

--- a/src/unix/nuttx.c
+++ b/src/unix/nuttx.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #include <unistd.h>
 
 #include <nuttx/tls.h>
+#include <nuttx/tls_task.h>
 
 int uv_exepath(char* buffer, size_t* size) {
